      "content": "It's true that the world can feel brutally unforgiving, and that sense of betrayal is profoundly heavy to carry. When everything feels gone, the sheer weight of starting over can feel impossible. Instead of thinking about rebuilding the whole foundation, perhaps you could focus on just one single, small thing to stand on right now. Even a tiny act of self-care or a single step toward a new routine can be a starting point when the whole structure feels like dust.",
      "source": "target",
